        "lessons": [
          {
            "title": "Lesson #1",
            "id": 148278,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Vamos aprender como usar funções para percorrer arrays e manipular seus valores sempre que quisermos, como quando pressionamos uma tecla em um jogo.</p><p>Execute o código abaixo que verifica se o valor <code>3</code> existe no array <code>enemyLevels</code> usando uma função.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" enemyLevels = [\" /><text value=\"1\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"3\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"2\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"5\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"3\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" search = \" /><text value=\"3\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"function\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"searchEnemyLevel\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"enemyLevels, search\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\") \" /><text value=\"{\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"for\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" (\" /><text value=\"let\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" i = \" /><text value=\"0\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"; i &lt; enemyLevels.length; i++) {\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"if\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" (enemyLevels[i] === search) {\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"   \" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(\" /><text value=\"&quot;Enemy level found!&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\");\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"   \" /><text value=\"break\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  }\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" }\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"}\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"searchEnemyLevel(enemyLevels, search);\" /></content></code></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #2",
            "id": 148279,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Funções são úteis quando queremos executar código reutilizável.</p><p>Para acessar os elementos do array usando a função <code>searchEnemyLevel</code>, vamos passar o array <code>enemyLevels</code> ao chamar a função.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"validatedInput\" startIndex=\"122\" endIndex=\"133\" isDefault=\"true\" /></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" enemyLevels = [\" /><text value=\"1\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"3\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"2\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"5\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"function\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"searchEnemyLevel\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"enemyLevels\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\") \" /><text value=\"{\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(enemyLevels);\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"}\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"searchEnemyLevel(enemyLevels);}\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Certifique-se de escolher <code>enemyLevels</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #3",
            "id": 148280,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Se quisermos acessar elementos armazenados em múltiplos arrays usando a mesma função, passamos os arrays como argumentos ao chamar a função.</p><p>Vamos codificar o segundo array <code>enemyLevels2</code> ao chamar <code>searchEnemyLevel()</code>.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"&amp;\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\":\" /></content></option><option startIndex=\"210\" endIndex=\"211\" /><option startIndex=\"212\" endIndex=\"224\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" enemyLevels = [\" /><text value=\"1\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"3\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"2\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"5\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" enemyLevels2 = [\" /><text value=\"2\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"4\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"1\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"6\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"function\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"searchEnemyLevel\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"enemyLevels, enemyLevels2\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\") \" /><text value=\"{\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(enemyLevels);\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(enemyLevels2);\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"}\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"searchEnemyLevel(enemyLevels, enemyLevels2);\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Certifique-se de escolher <code>,</code> seguido de <code>enemyLevels2</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #4",
            "id": 148281,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Uma vez que passamos um array para uma função, podemos iterar sobre os elementos do array. Crie um loop <code>for</code> para iterar por todos os elementos.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\" name=\"script.js\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" enemyLevels = [\" /><text value=\"1\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"3\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"2\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"5\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"function\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"searchEnemyLevel\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"enemyLevels\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\") \" /><text value=\"{\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" len = enemyLevels.length;\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"for\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" (\" /><text value=\"let\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" i = \" /><text value=\"0\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"; i &lt; len; i++) {}\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"}\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"searchEnemyLevel(enemyLevels);\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"while\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"{\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"}\" /></content></option><option startIndex=\"110\" endIndex=\"113\" /><option startIndex=\"114\" endIndex=\"115\" /><option startIndex=\"138\" endIndex=\"139\" /></options></interaction></interactions></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Certifique-se de escolher <code>for</code> seguido de <code>(</code> e finalmente <code>)</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #5",
            "id": 148282,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Para recuperar cada elemento do array dentro de um loop <code>for</code>, usamos a sintaxe <code>array[i]</code>, onde <code>i</code> é a iteração atual, e <code>array</code> é o nome do array.</p><p>Vamos escrever o código para recuperar elementos individuais de <code>enemyLevels</code>.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"validatedInput\" startIndex=\"138\" endIndex=\"152\" isDefault=\"true\" /></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" enemyLevels = [\" /><text value=\"1\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"3\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"2\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"5\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"function\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"searchEnemyLevel\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"enemyLevels\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\") \" /><text value=\"{\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"for\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" (\" /><text value=\"let\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" i = \" /><text value=\"0\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"; i &lt; enemyLevels.length; i++) {\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(enemyLevels[i]);\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" }\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"}\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"searchEnemyLevel(enemyLevels);}\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Certifique-se de escolher <code>enemyLevels[i]</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #6",
            "id": 148283,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Usando uma função, um array e outro parâmetro, podemos fazer muito.</p><p>Por exemplo, vamos procurar o elemento <code>3</code> no array <code>enemyLevels</code> passando <code>enemyLevels</code> e depois <code>search</code> para a função <code>searchEnemyLevel</code>.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"&amp;\" /></content></option><option startIndex=\"262\" endIndex=\"273\" /><option startIndex=\"273\" endIndex=\"274\" /><option startIndex=\"275\" endIndex=\"281\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" enemyLevels = [\" /><text value=\"1\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"3\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"2\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"5\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"3\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" search = \" /><text value=\"3\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"function\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"searchEnemyLevel\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"enemyLevels, search\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\") \" /><text value=\"{\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"for\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" (\" /><text value=\"let\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" i = \" /><text value=\"0\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"; i &lt; enemyLevels.length; i++) {\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"if\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" (enemyLevels[i] === search) {\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"   \" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(\" /><text value=\"&quot;Enemy level found!&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\");\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"   \" /><text value=\"break\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  }\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" }\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"}\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"searchEnemyLevel(enemyLevels, search);\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Certifique-se de escolher <code>enemyLevels</code> seguido de <code>,</code> e finalmente <code>search</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #7",
            "id": 148284,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Também podemos usar múltiplos arrays com uma função para realizar uma ação específica, como encontrar elementos comuns de arrays.</p><p>Vamos encontrar elementos comuns em dois arrays passando-os para a função <code>compareArrays</code>.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"validatedInput\" startIndex=\"263\" endIndex=\"271\" isDefault=\"true\" /></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" one = [\" /><text value=\"100\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"80\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"60\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"40\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"20\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" two = [\" /><text value=\"90\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"80\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"55\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"40\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"10\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"function\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"compareArrays\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"one, two\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\") \" /><text value=\"{\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"for\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" (\" /><text value=\"let\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" i = \" /><text value=\"0\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"; i &lt; one.length; i++) {\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"if\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" (one[i] === two[i]) {\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"   \" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(\" /><text value=\"&quot;Same value at this index:&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", one[i]);\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  }\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" }\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"return\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"false\" class=\"literal\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"}\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"compareArrays(one, two);}\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Certifique-se de escolher <code>one, two</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #8",
            "id": 148285,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Como acessamos elementos de um array dentro de uma função?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">Nós passamos o array para a função</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">Nós chamamos o array diretamente sem passá-lo para a função</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Nós passamos o array para a função.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #9",
            "id": 148286,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>O que este código exibe no console?</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" playerNames = [\" /><text value=\"&quot;Rin&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;Kai&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" playerScores = [\" /><text value=\"2500\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"3100\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"function\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"displayPlayers\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"playerNames, playerScores\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\") \" /><text value=\"{\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(playerNames);\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(playerScores);\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"}\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"displayPlayers(playerNames, playerScores);\" /></content></code><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">Ele exibe múltiplos arrays</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">Ele exibe apenas o primeiro array</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Ele exibe múltiplos arrays.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #10",
            "id": 148287,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>O que podemos usar dentro de uma função para iterar sobre um array passado para a função?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">Podemos usar um loop <code>for</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">Podemos usar uma declaração <code>if</code></item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Podemos usar um loop <code>for</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #11",
            "id": 148288,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>O que acontece quando usamos <code>playerNames[i]</code> dentro de um <code>for</code> loop como na função abaixo?</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" playerNames = [\" /><text value=\"&quot;Rin&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;Kai&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"function\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"searchPlayer\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"playerNames\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\") \" /><text value=\"{\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"for\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" (\" /><text value=\"let\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" i = \" /><text value=\"0\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"; i &lt; playerNames.length; i++) {\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(playerNames[i]);\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" }\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"}\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"searchPlayer(playerNames);\" /></content></code><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">Nós recuperamos os elementos do array um por um</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">Nós recuperamos os elementos do array de uma só vez</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Nós recuperamos os elementos do array um por um.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #12",
            "id": 148289,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>O que este código exibe no console?</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" items = [\" /><text value=\"&quot;Potion&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;Key&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" search = \" /><text value=\"&quot;Gem&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"function\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"searchItem\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"items, search\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\") \" /><text value=\"{\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"for\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" (\" /><text value=\"let\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" i = \" /><text value=\"0\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"; i &lt; items.length; i++) {\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"if\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" (items[i] == search) {\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"   \" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(\" /><text value=\"&quot;The item exists!&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\");\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"   \" /><text value=\"break\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  }\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" }\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"}\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"searchItem(items, search);\" /></content></code><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">Não exibe nada</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">Ele exibe <code>The item exists!</code></item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Não exibe nada.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
